    <string name="permissions_reviewer_body1">A second AI model checks actions against what you asked before they run. It sees your recent messages and the action, </string>
    <string name="permissions_reviewer_body2">never web pages, emails or files the agent read. Anything it isn\'t sure about comes to you, and Deny below always wins.</string>
    <string name="permissions_tools_body">Allow runs without asking. Ask shows you each action first. Deny blocks the tool.</string>
    <string name="permissions_sensitive_note">Some actions, like sensitive clicks in the browser, always ask regardless of these settings.</string>
    <string name="permissions_remembered_body1">Answers you gave with “This chat” or “Always” on an approval card. Each covers one tool and one site, folder, </string>
    <string name="permissions_remembered_body2">recipient or command. “Always” lasts 30 days. Deny, project limits, payments and the reviewer still win.</string>
    <string name="permissions_nothing_remembered_body">Every action set to Ask asks you.</string>
    <string name="permissions_reviewer_outward_body">Sending email, deploying, paying and similar. Off: these always come to you.</string>
    <string name="permissions_ask_actions_body">Actions set to Ask always ask you.</string>
    <string name="permissions_reviewer_mode_body">Checks actions set to Ask: runs the clearly fine ones, blocks the clearly wrong ones, asks you about the rest. Uses $model.</string>
    <string name="permissions_reviewer_all_changes_body">Also checks allowed actions that change something; any it doesn\'t clear come to you. Uses $model.</string>
